# 7. Backtest UI

All explanatory text must be Vietnamese.

Examples:

Backtest Summary → Tổng quan Backtest

Dataset → Bộ dữ liệu

Performance → Hiệu suất

Trade Statistics → Thống kê giao dịch

Execution Assumptions → Giả định khớp lệnh

Data Quality → Chất lượng dữ liệu

Interpretation → Diễn giải

Historical Simulation → Mô phỏng lịch sử

Insufficient Data → Dữ liệu chưa đủ

Research Only → Chỉ dùng cho mục đích nghiên cứu

---

# 8. Error Messages

Human-readable errors must be Vietnamese.

Example:

Bad:

"Failed to load positions."

Good:

"Không thể tải danh sách vị thế."

Bad:

"No backtest reports found."

Good:

"Chưa có báo cáo Backtest nào."

Bad:

"Invalid date range."

Good:

"Khoảng thời gian không hợp lệ."

Technical error details may remain in English when they are intended for developers/logging.

---

# 9. Logs

Separate:

## Operator-facing logs

Vietnamese.

Example:

"Đã kết nối thành công với MT5."

"Không tìm thấy dữ liệu XAUUSD M15."

## Developer/debug logs

Technical English is allowed.

Example:

"Failed to initialize MT5 client"

Do not force Vietnamese into stack traces, exception names, library errors, or technical diagnostics.

---

# 10. Documentation

Human-readable project documentation should be written in Vietnamese by default.

This includes:

docs/

and:

trading-engine/docs/

Technical identifiers, code snippets, API fields, commands, configuration keys, and library names remain unchanged.

English terminology may be retained when it is the standard technical term and translating it would reduce clarity.

Example:

"Backtest sử dụng dữ liệu XAUUSD M15."

is preferred over forcing an unnatural translation of "Backtest".

---

# 11. Code Comments

Prefer Vietnamese for explanatory comments written for project maintainers.

Example:

Good:

// Không kiểm tra SL/TP trên candle vào lệnh để tránh sai lệch backtest.

Avoid unnecessary comments.

Do not translate:

* third-party comments
* generated code
* library code
* copied protocol specifications

---

# 12. SEO / Metadata

For the Dashboard, use Vietnamese for:

* page titles
* descriptions
* metadata
* accessible labels
* aria-label
* tooltips

Example:

title:
"Bảng điều khiển giao dịch"

description:
"Theo dõi trạng thái Bot, vị thế, rủi ro và hiệu suất Backtest."

---

# 13. Accessibility

Accessibility text must also be Vietnamese.

Examples:

"Đóng menu"

"Mở bộ lọc"

"Đang tải dữ liệu"

"Biểu đồ vốn theo thời gian"

"Không có vị thế đang mở"

Do not leave English accessibility labels unless they are technical identifiers.

---

# 14. Mock Data

Mock data intended for UI display must use Vietnamese text.

Example:

Good:

{
exitReasonLabel: "Chốt lời"
}

Technical value may remain:

{
exitReason: "TAKE_PROFIT"
}

Keep domain values stable.

Translate only presentation labels.

---

# 15. Separation of Technical Value and Display Label

Prefer this pattern:

const STATUS_LABELS = {
RUNNING: "Đang chạy",
STOPPED: "Đã dừng",
ERROR: "Lỗi",
DISCONNECTED: "Mất kết nối",
}

Do NOT change:

RUNNING

to:

DANG_CHAY

The internal value remains English/technical.

Only the presentation layer translates it.

---

# 16. No Mixed-Language UI

Avoid unnecessary mixed-language UI.

Bad:

"Open Positions"

"Today PnL"

"Risk Limit"

Good:

"Vị thế đang mở"

"PnL hôm nay"

"Giới hạn rủi ro"

Technical trading terms that are commonly used in Vietnamese may remain:

* PnL
* Backtest
* EMA
* RSI
* ATR
* MT5
* XAUUSD
* Spread
* Swap
* Slippage

---

# 17. Existing Code

Before modifying existing UI text:

1. Search the entire dashboard for user-facing English strings.
2. Translate them into Vietnamese.
3. Preserve technical identifiers.
4. Preserve API/domain values.
5. Preserve route paths.
6. Preserve CLI commands.
7. Preserve environment variable names.

Do not perform a blind global replacement.

Review each occurrence based on context.

---

# 18. Future Internationalization

Do not implement a full i18n system in this phase unless the existing project already has one.

However, structure presentation labels so that introducing i18n later is straightforward.

Avoid scattering duplicated user-facing strings across many components.

Where appropriate, centralize:

* status labels
* trading direction labels
* exit reason labels
* navigation labels
* common UI labels

---

# 19. Source Code Language

Source code itself may remain English.

Examples:

Keep:

getBacktestReports()
formatCurrency()
BacktestSummary
RiskCard
PositionTable

Do NOT translate code identifiers into Vietnamese.

---

# 20. Final Rule

Vietnamese is the default language for humans.

English is allowed and preferred for:

* code
* identifiers
* protocols
* APIs
* technical values
* library names
* market symbols
* standard technical terminology
* developer diagnostics

The rule can be summarized as:

HUMAN-FACING CONTENT → VIETNAMESE

TECHNICAL IDENTIFIERS → KEEP ORIGINAL

DOMAIN VALUES → KEEP STABLE

PRESENTATION LABELS → VIETNAMESE
